=== Zodiac Stats ===

Zodiac Stat Formula:
<pre>
Mults Gain          = 1.35^x
Prom Power          = 1.2^log(x)
Common Exponent     = 1 + log(x) * 0.016
Ascension Power     = 1.5^log(x)
Laps Speed          = 2^log(x)
Slowdown Power      = round(log(x + 9)^1.5)
IP Gain             = 1 + log(x) * 0.025
Infinity Gain       = 3^log(x)
Gen Exponent        = 1 + log(x) * 0.024
Mult Per Bought Gen = 1 + log(x) * 0.007
Star Base           = 1.8^log(x)
Stardust Exponent   = 1 + log(x) * 0.02
Eternity Gain       = 2^log(x)
EP Gain             = 1 + log(x) * 0.011
Lab Mult Power      = 1 + log(x) * 0.012
Supernova Req       = 1 / (1 + log(x) * 0.02)
DP Gain             = 1 + log(x) * 0.05
Free Lab Levels     = round(log(x + 9)^3 * 5)
DTP Cost            = 1 / (1 + log(x) * 0.015)
Center DTU Eff      = 1 + log(x) * 0.02
Ach 29 Reward       = 1 + log(x) * 0.005
Game Speed          = 1 + log(x) * 0.1
Luck Add            = log((x / 20)^0.45 * 20) * 0.07
Zodiac Quality Mult = 1 + log(x) * 0.04
</pre>

where:

<pre>
x = Zodiac Score = 1.125^ZodiacRarity * ZodiacQuality * (9 + ZodiacLevel^2) * 2 * ((ZodiacLevel - 90) / 10) ^ 2.5
</pre>

and:

<pre>
ZodiacRarity = Immo+ Number + 9
</pre>


=== Zodiac Luck ===

<math>\begin{cases}
Luck< 18: & ZodiacLuck=Luck\\
Luck\geqslant 18: & ZodiacLuck=\left(\frac{Luck}{18}\right)^{0.3} \times 18
\end{cases}</math>
Zodiac luck is an internal variable that is just Luck with a soft cap after 18.

=== Rarity Weight ===
Rarity "Weight" (unofficial name) is a value derived from Zodiac Luck that is used to calculate the chance for each rarity.

Garbage weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 2: & Weight = 5 \times 0.8^{(ZodiacLuck - 1)}\\
2 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 3: & Weight = 5 \times 0.8^{(ZodiacLuck - 1)} \times 0.4^{(ZodiacLuck - 2)}\\
3 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:       & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Common weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 2: & Weight = 15\\
2 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 5: & Weight = 15 \times 0.45^{(ZodiacLuck - 2)}\\
5 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:      & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Uncommon weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 3: & Weight = 20 \times 1.5^{(ZodiacLuck - 1)} - 12\\
3 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 8: & Weight = \bigl(20 \times 1.5^{(ZodiacLuck - 1)} - 12\bigr) \times 0.5^{(ZodiacLuck - 3)}\\
8 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:      & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Rare weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 5:  & Weight = 30 \times 1.45^{(ZodiacLuck - 1)} - 28\\
5 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 12: & Weight = \bigl(30 \times 1.45^{(ZodiacLuck - 1)} - 28\bigr) \times 0.55^{(ZodiacLuck - 5)}\\
12 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:     & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Epic weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 8:  & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;45 \times 1.4^{(ZodiacLuck - 2)} - 50\bigr)\\
8 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 20: & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;45 \times 1.4^{(ZodiacLuck - 2)} - 50\bigr)\times 0.6^{(ZodiacLuck - 8)}\\
20 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:     & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Legendary weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 12:  & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;80 \times 1.36^{(ZodiacLuck - 3)} - 100\bigr)\\
12 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 30: & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;80 \times 1.36^{(ZodiacLuck - 3)} - 100\bigr)\times 0.64^{(ZodiacLuck - 12)}\\
30 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:      & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Mythic weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 20:  & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;120 \times 1.3^{(ZodiacLuck - 5)} - 140\bigr)\\
20 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 50: & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;120 \times 1.3^{(ZodiacLuck - 5)} - 140\bigr)\times 0.67^{(ZodiacLuck - 20)}\\
50 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:      & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Godly weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 30:  & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;150 \times 1.25^{(ZodiacLuck - 8)} - 200\bigr)\\
30 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 60: & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;150 \times 1.25^{(ZodiacLuck - 8)} - 200\bigr)\times 0.7^{(ZodiacLuck - 30)}\\
60 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:      & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>

Divine weight:

<math>
\begin{cases}
1 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 40:  & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;200 \times 1.2^{(ZodiacLuck - 12)} - 300\bigr)\\
40 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 50: & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;200 \times 1.2^{(ZodiacLuck - 12)} - 300\bigr)\times 0.92^{(ZodiacLuck - 40)}\\
50 \leqslant ZodiacLuck < 70: & Weight = \max\bigl(0,\;200 \times 1.2^{(ZodiacLuck - 12)} - 300\bigr)\times 0.92^{(ZodiacLuck - 40)}\times 0.75^{(ZodiacLuck - 50)}\\
70 \leqslant ZodiacLuck:      & Weight = 0
\end{cases}
</math>


Immortal weight:

<math>
\text{Weight} \;=\;\max\bigl(0,\;300 \times 1.1^{(ZodiacLuck - 20)} \;-\; 500\bigr)
</math>

=== Rarity Chance ===
The chance that a given rarity is chosen is the fraction that its weight makes of all weights combined.
 Chance(this Rarity) = Weight(this Rarity) / Sum(all rarity weights)

